{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04R5", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nU' \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & V' \\ar[d] \\\\\nU \\ar[r] & V\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$v' \\in V'$", "MATH_0003": "$v \\in V$", "MATH_0004": "$U'_{v'} \\to U_v$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-on-fiber}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:413141d7c4fa397c1a9abb4922a58a6d5e6e3af0ca196b0ad34bf64b2808576c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8cbc59f736f395db0c4b280900a7174276b713a1f65910de65248d04afdbaba4", "source_text": "Consider a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes\n<MATH_0001>\nwith <ACCENT_0001>tale vertical arrows and a point <MATH_0002> mapping to <MATH_0003>.\nThen the morphism of fibres <MATH_0004> is <ACCENT_0002>tale.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f31e49546a398d551719d1c5a916a405076c6cf13885a4ee32bb057374efbea", "unit_id": "tag:04NI:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04R5", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U'_v \\to U_v$", "MATH_0002": "$U' \\to U$", "MATH_0003": "$U'_v$", "MATH_0004": "$V'_v$", "MATH_0005": "$V'_v$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa(v)$", "MATH_0007": "$v' = \\Spec(\\kappa(v'))$", "MATH_0008": "$U'_{v'}$", "MATH_0009": "$U'_v$", "MATH_0010": "$U'_{v'} \\to U'_v \\to U_v$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-etale-over-field}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-section-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:511be6378a6428bfd3ab0b6ed9d6b39b6f6ffaff2caa8ae7f05d4dab3f9d75ed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd55e2e17269decdd47844bd3589162bb21a400f3034618334788930c102bb68", "source_text": "Note that <MATH_0001> is <ACCENT_0001>tale as a base change of the <ACCENT_0002>tale\nmorphism <MATH_0002>. The scheme <MATH_0003> is a scheme over <MATH_0004>. By\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe scheme <MATH_0005> is a disjoint union of spectra\nof finite separable field extensions of <MATH_0006>.\nOne of these is <MATH_0007>. Hence\n<MATH_0008> is an open and closed subscheme of <MATH_0009> and it follows\nthat <MATH_0010> is <ACCENT_0003>tale (as a composition of an\nopen immersion and an <ACCENT_0004>tale morphism, see\nMorphisms, Section <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e2e629693d46ed38bb94d549bd0aab39fe709327f7f7c0cb431b4305f4f8de67", "unit_id": "tag:04NI:proof"}
